# PRIMES-LOOP  -  endless prime-number enumerator for the Busch Microtronic 2090
#
# Shows the primes 2, 3, 5, 7, ... 997 and then starts again at 2.
#
# After RUN it waits for ONE key: the pause after each prime, 0 to F
# (about one second per unit; 0 = no pause).
#
# The display stays on the last prime found while the next one is searched,
# and the output LEDs flicker with the trial divisor.
#
# Fully commented source: PRIMES-LOOP.asm.  Written by Claude Code (Opus 5.5), October 2026.

